{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1475933-slashers-as-antagonists","id":1475933,"title":"Slashers as antagonists?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-06T13:48:05-08:00","id":1475933,"title":"Slashers as antagonists?","content":"With vigil 2e out, and slashers getting updated, I had this visual of a pack hunting a murder only to find he won\u2019t die. How would you implement a slasher? Would you run it as a claimed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T14:05:28-08:00","id":1475936,"title":"","content":"As in, using solely Werewolf 2e rules to stat slashers? Then yeah, Claimed seem to be the best fit. Maybe with a Facet or two to give them a power boost or emphasize \u201cthis one\u2019s Not The Usual sort\u201d. <br /> <br /> Although, I don\u2019t remember Werewolf having guides for building corporeal monsters other than \u201cimprovise\u201d or \u201cwing it\u201d\u2026 backporting Hunter 2e\u2019s Horror rules (or just the CofD core\u2019s one) may be worth considering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T14:08:41-08:00","id":1475938,"title":"","content":"Well that could be a thing, however I have hunter so I was thinking of running one of those slashers. I\u2019ve liked the concept for a hot minute. Vigil 2e is also pretty damn fantastic from what I\u2019m seeing so far. <br /> <br /> The horror rules though, that may be the vibe I\u2019m looking for. I can\u2019t do any of this just yet as my current forsaken game has the players pitted against an idigam. I\u2019m not wanting to over saturate the field.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-31T07:47:47-07:00","id":1477766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1475933-slashers-as-antagonists#post1475933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With vigil 2e out, and slashers getting updated, I had this visual of a pack hunting a murder only to find he won\u2019t die. How would you implement a slasher? Would you run it as a claimed?</div> </div> </div> </div>No claimed needes. Pure slasher. Most likely Maniac or Psycho for the spiritual desolation they can leave behind their actions. A smart Maniac or Psycho could be a though opponent that can comes out from a side quest. Despite a single uratha can easily rip apart a slasher, a Maniac targeting human members of the pack or wolf blooded could be a very dangerous opponent. He can even turning pack against pack, and from hunter2 you can boost him with dread powers","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-05T16:49:42-07:00","id":1478100,"title":"","content":"One interesting take to boost a Slasher's &quot;power&quot; in a Forsaken game without really making them something else is to go for the effect they have on the Shadow.<br /> <br /> Slashers are completely out of the ordinary, so it makes perfect sense that they have extraordinary effects in the spiritual landscape for a single person. Change the Essence in the area, make them generate certain kinds of Essence almost as (or even better than) living Loci, suppress some sorts of Essence, alter how other people and even things generate Essence after interacting with a Slasher.<br /> <br /> When you think the background of a place or thing to be a Locus, have a strong resonance or even be a Wound, Slashers are the kind of actor that are pictured when things happened in a Blaze of G(l)ory instead of through untold years. It makes sense for how Spirits, Essence and the Shadow work to have such characters being a huge deal even if their personal capacity is strictly what's in Hunter, and makes them relevant for Werewolves to deal with (after figuring out what the fuck is going on).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-05T17:01:44-07:00","id":1478102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1475933-slashers-as-antagonists?p=1478100#post1478100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One interesting take to boost a Slasher's &amp;quot;power&amp;quot; in a Forsaken game without really making them something else is to go for the effect they have on the Shadow.<br /> <br /> Slashers are completely out of the ordinary, so it makes perfect sense that they have extraordinary effects in the spiritual landscape for a single person. Change the Essence in the area, make them generate certain kinds of Essence almost as (or even better than) living Loci, suppress some sorts of Essence, alter how other people and even things generate Essence after interacting with a Slasher.<br /> <br /> When you think the background of a place or thing to be a Locus, have a strong resonance or even be a Wound, Slashers are the kind of actor that are pictured when things happened in a Blaze of G(l)ory instead of through untold years. It makes sense for how Spirits, Essence and the Shadow work to have such characters being a huge deal even if their personal capacity is strictly what's in Hunter, and makes them relevant for Werewolves to deal with (after figuring out what the fuck is going on).</div> </div> </div> </div>A Slasher turning out to be a walking Locus/Wound could really be \u2018fun\u2019. We get to have \u2018boss battles\u2019 where the \u2018boss\u2019 summons its flunkies (spirits), and the boss itself goes one-winged angel as Round Two (Claiming and/or whatever it is that fiends can do) !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}